# XeFM Microsoft Store (MSIX) identity configuration (template).
#
# Copy this file to `store.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in your values:
#
#     copy store.env.example store.env
#
# build_msix.ps1 loads store.env automatically, so you don't have to pass the
# three identity flags on every pack. Anything passed explicitly on the command
# line (-IdentityName / -Publisher / -PublisherDisplayName) overrides what's here.
#
# NOTE: None of these is a secret -- all three are embedded in, and readable
# from, every published package. They are kept out of git because they are tied
# to one Partner Center account, so a fork must supply its own rather than
# silently inheriting ours. Without this file the build falls back to a
# `XeFM.Prototype` identity that packs and sideloads fine but cannot be submitted.
#
# Find all three in Partner Center under your reserved product ->
# Product management -> Product identity ("製品 ID"). Copy them VERBATIM; the
# Store rejects a package whose identity does not match the reservation.
# See doc/dev/WINDOWS_STORE_MSIX_PLAN.md 2a.

# Package/Identity/Name -- "<PublisherId>.<AppName>", e.g. contoso.XeFM
XEFM_MSIX_IDENTITY_NAME="YourPublisherId.XeFM"

# Package/Identity/Publisher -- your publisher GUID, including the CN= prefix.
XEFM_MSIX_PUBLISHER="CN=XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX"

# Package/Properties/PublisherDisplayName -- your display name as shown on the
# Store listing.
XEFM_MSIX_PUBLISHER_DISPLAY_NAME="Your Publisher Display Name"
